# Engineered by Dhanush C N (github.com/dhanush-cn)
#
# Without this file the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` copies the HOST node_modules
# over the one `npm ci` just installed in the image. That is fatal rather than
# merely wasteful: node_modules here was installed on Windows, so it carries
# @rolldown/binding-win32-x64-msvc and no Linux binding, and `npm run build`
# inside the alpine builder dies with "Cannot find native binding".
#
# It also keeps the build context small — the context is uploaded to the Docker
# daemon on every build, and node_modules alone is a few hundred megabytes.
node_modules
dist
dist-demo
dist-ssr
coverage

# Screenshots are documentation; nginx only ever serves dist/.
docs

.git
.gitignore
*.log
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
